### 1. Health endpoint is public
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health

###

### 2. Ticket endpoint without token returns 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets

###

### 3. Register user returns token
# @name register
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Day9 Demo User",
  "email": "day9demo@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### 4. Login user returns token
# @name loginUser
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "day9demo@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### 5. Ticket endpoint with token returns 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.$.token}}

###

### 6. Create ticket with normal USER token returns 403
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should be blocked",
  "description": "USER role cannot create tickets",
  "category": "Network",
  "priority": "LOW",
  "createdBy": "day9demo@example.com"
}

###

### 7. Login admin returns token
# @name loginAdmin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@123"
}

###

### 8. Create ticket with ADMIN token returns 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Should be allowed",
  "description": "ADMIN role can create tickets",
  "category": "Network",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "createdBy": "admin@example.com"
}
